    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a8">

                <pb facs="0085" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg35"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 92.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Karel to Mr.
                            Townsend.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The governor of Bohemia has dismissed the
                    appeal of David Hofmann on the ground that he did not appeal within the time
                    prescribed by law, namely, within three days. I am sorry; I would like to have
                    heard the governor’s ruling on this question.</p>
                <p>A copy of the decision is herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have written to Mr. Hofmann that under these circumstances he will have to
                    leave.</p>
                <p>Will you bring it before the imperial and royal minister of foreign affairs?</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Karel.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
